            <ArticleTitle>A class of pyrrole derivatives endowed with analgesic/anti-inflammatory activity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3695-701</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmc.2013.04.031</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0968-0896(13)00357-X</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the synthesis and bio-pharmacological evaluation of a class of pyrrole derivatives featuring a small appendage fragment (carbaldehyde, oxime, nitrile) on the central core. Compound 1c proved to be extremely effective in vivo, showing an interesting anti-nociceptic profile that is comparable to reference compounds already marketed, hence representing a great stimulus for a further improvement of this class of molecules.</AbstractText>
